From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] host: byte equality by indexOfDiff, and a string index that stops counting at it

Fork ai-engine, ref fork-ssh/ovn-up, commit ef81b4a49 "server: render and
tokenize a request once; TF_GLM_OVN_HOST_ONCE": the two standalone measured
optimisations inside it. The rest of that commit is the next two patches.

memo.equal: the tokenizer's segment cache confirms a hit by comparing the
stored bytes with the caller's. The fork replaced std.mem.eql with
std.mem.indexOfDiff and kept the measurement in the comment above it, 0.23 ms
against 2.1 ms on 1.4 MB. Both call sites take it, the one in append and the
one in same. The two forms agree on every input: indexOfDiff returns null
exactly when the slices are equal.

access.strIndex: a chat template reading content.0 makes getitem evaluate
index(i, uni.count(s.s)), which walks the whole string before indexing its
first code point. strIndex walks only as far as the requested index for a
non-negative one and falls back to the counted form for a negative one. The
fork's own randomised test comes with it: 2,000 strings of mixed ASCII,
multi-byte and malformed bytes, every index from -n-2 to n+2 compared against
index(i, uni.count(s)).

No patch in this stack touches either file, so this completes nothing earlier;
it is the first piece of the fork's host-side work to land here.

What is not the fork's own lines, and why:
- memo.zig is the fork's hunk applied as it stands.
- access.zig is hand-placed. The fork's hunk carries getitem's list arm as
  l.items.len and l.items[k] where the pin has l.count() and l.at(k), so the
  hunk is refused and only the str arm's call site changes here. strIndex and
  its test are the fork's lines unchanged.
- the fuzz test needs a binary that runs it. template.zig's test block gains
  the access.zig import, and zig/build/cuda.zig puts the template module in
  the list of modules whose own tests test-cuda-host runs, which is the fork's
  change to that line. In our tree the template module is built by
  cuda_server_host.zig and returned to that caller, so the list is the only
  edit needed. Before this the chat template's own tests ran in the macOS
  build alone; the 36 they add all pass here.

What a GPU run has to say: nothing about correctness. Both changes are
host-side and leave ids and rendered text identical, which the tokenizer and
template host tests prove. A serve receipt would only show time saved, and the
time this commit was written for arrives with patch 03.

Re-seated on v1.2.7 (93a2e93ecebff8aa52b88e58c5dd222516e69c5f, from pin 9c9bf542) by the 2026-11-12 re-seat (work/reseat/DECISIONS.md):
- memo.zig: a56c63daf set min_bytes to 64 ("keep segments of 64 bytes or more, not 1,024"); the 3-way merge keeps v1.2.7's 64 and takes the fold's std.mem.indexOfDiff at both call sites.
- zig/build/cuda.zig: the template module joins the test list on v1.2.7's line, whose cuda_server_host.steps call gained build_options.
- source: work/fold/0034-memo-equal-strindex.patch

